{title: Money Money Money }
{artist: ABBA}
{subtitle: v1 Key: Am, Tempo: 230}
{key: Am}
{tempo: 230}
{duration: 3:47}
{define-ukulele: E7#5 base-fret 0 frets 1 2 0 3}
{define-ukulele: F7 base-fret 0 frets 2 3 1 3}

{start_of_grid: Intro}
| Am .  . | F7 . . | Dm  E7#5 . | Am . . |
{end_of_grid}


{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
I [Am]work all night, I work all day to [E7/G#]pay the bills I have to pay,
[E7]     ... ain't it sad.[Am]
And [Am]still there never seems to be a [E7/G#]single penny left for me
[E7]     ... that's too bad.[Am]
[Dm]In my [Am]dreams I [E7]have a [Am]plan,[G]
[F]  if I got me a wealthy man
I [Dm]wouldn't have to work at all, I'd [B7/D#]fool around and have a ball[E7].
[E7]////     [E7]////
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus 1}
[Am]Money, money, money, [B7]   must be funny
[Dm]   in the [E7#5]rich man's [Am]world. [E7]
[Am]Money, money, money, [B7]   always sunny,
[Dm]   in the [E7#5]rich man's [Am]world.
A-[Dm]ha,     a-[E7]ha.
[A7]   All the things I could [Dm]do,      [F]if [E7]I
[Am]had a little money,
[Dm]   It's a [E7#5]rich man's [Am]world.     [F7]
[Dm]   It's a [E7#5]rich man's [Am]world.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
A [Am]man like that is hard to find but [E7/G#]I can't get him off my mind,
[E7]     ...ain't it [Am]sad.
And [Am]if he happens to be free I [E7/G#]bet he wouldn't fancy me,
[E7]     ...that's too bad[Am].
So [Dm]I must [Am]leave, I'll [E7]have to go [Am].[G]
[F] To Las Vegas or Monaco
And [Dm]win a fortune in a game, my [B7/D#]life will never be the same...[E7]
[E7]////     [E7]////
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus 2}
